#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:4
msgid "Lyapunov exponent computation"
msgstr "Cálculo de expoentes de Lyapunov"

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:7
msgid "Motivation"
msgstr "Motivação"

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:9
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"In chaotic dynamics, the **largest Lyapunov exponent** "
":math:`\\lambda_{\\max}` quantifies how quickly two initially nearby "
"trajectories diverge from each other.  If :math:`\\lambda_{\\max} > 0`, "
"the system is chaotic: a tiny perturbation in the initial condition grows"
" exponentially and the long-term behaviour becomes unpredictable.  If "
":math:`\\lambda_{\\max} \\le 0`, the system is periodic or stable."
msgstr ""
"In chaotic dynamics, the **largest Lyapunov exponent** "
":math:`\\lambda_{\\max}` quantifies how quickly two initially nearby "
"trajectories diverge from each other.  If :math:`\\lambda_{\\max} > 0`, "
"the system is chaotic — a tiny perturbation in the initial condition "
"grows exponentially and the long-term behaviour becomes unpredictable.  "
"If :math:`\\lambda_{\\max} \\le 0`, the system is periodic or stable."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:16
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For chaotic communication, :math:`\\lambda_{\\max}` is the single most "
"important diagnostic: it tells us whether the Hénon map with a given FIR "
"filter still preserves chaos, or whether the filter *killed* the chaos "
"(making the scheme useless for physical-layer security)."
msgstr "Para a comunicação caótica, :math:`\\lambda_{\\max}` é o diagnóstico isolado mais importante: informa se o mapa de Hénon com um dado filtro FIR ainda preserva o caos, ou se o filtro *matou* o caos (tornando o esquema inútil para segurança na camada física)."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:22
msgid "Mathematical definition"
msgstr "Definição matemática"

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:24
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For a discrete-time dynamical system :math:`\\mathbf{x}_{n+1} = "
"f(\\mathbf{x}_n)`, the largest Lyapunov exponent is defined as the time-"
"averaged exponential divergence rate:"
msgstr "Para um sistema dinâmico de tempo discreto :math:`\\mathbf{x}_{n+1} = f(\\mathbf{x}_n)`, o maior expoente de Lyapunov é definido como a taxa média temporal de divergência exponencial:"

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:28
msgid ""
"\\lambda_{\\max}\n"
"= \\lim_{N \\to \\infty} \\frac{1}{N}\n"
"  \\sum_{k=1}^{N} \\ln \\frac{\\| \\delta \\mathbf{x}_k \\|}\n"
"                            {\\| \\delta \\mathbf{x}_{k-1} \\|},"
msgstr ""
"\\lambda_{\\max}\\n= \\lim_{N \\to \\infty} \\frac{1}{N}\\n  "
"\\sum_{k=1}^{N} \\ln \\frac{\\| \\delta \\mathbf{x}_k \\|}\\n"
"                            {\\| \\delta \\mathbf{x}_{k-1} \\|},"

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:35
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where :math:`\\delta \\mathbf{x}_k` is the evolved tangent vector at step"
" :math:`k`, obtained by applying the Jacobian :math:`J(\\mathbf{x}_k)` "
"and re-normalising."
msgstr "onde :math:`\\delta \\mathbf{x}_k` é o vetor tangente evoluído no passo :math:`k`, obtido aplicando a Jacobiana :math:`J(\\mathbf{x}_k)` e renormalizando."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:39
msgid ""
"In the code, this is the **\"Gram-Schmidt\"** (more precisely, **Modified"
" Gram-Schmidt  (MGS)**) approach to Lyapunov spectra.  The MGS variant is"
" more stable numerically than classical Gram-Schmidt, especially when the"
" tangent vectors become nearly parallel after many iterations."
msgstr ""
"In the code, this is the **\\** (more precisely, **Modified Gram-Schmidt "
"— MGS**) approach to Lyapunov spectra.  The MGS variant is more stable "
"numerically than classical Gram-Schmidt, especially when the tangent "
"vectors become nearly parallel after many iterations."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:44
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The **production sweeps do not use the full MGS**, though: to keep the "
"cost :math:`\\mathcal{O}(K)` per iteration instead of "
":math:`\\mathcal{O}(K^3)`, the sweep kernel propagates a **single tangent"
" vector**, multiplied by the Jacobian at each step and renormalised once "
"every **ten** iterations (a period that follows the established practice "
"of Benettin *et al.*).  The full-spectrum MGS above is used by the "
"validation wrappers and, in the sweep, to recompute the *marginal* cells "
"(:math:`|\\lambda| < 5\\times10^{-3}`) whose class the single-vector "
"estimate cannot settle confidently (``fallback_mode=1``)."
msgstr ""
"Os **sweeps de produção não usam o MGS completo**, porém: para manter o "
"custo O(K) por iteração em vez de O(K^3), o kernel da varredura propaga "
"um **único vetor tangente**, multiplicado pela Jacobiana a cada passo e "
"renormalizado uma vez a cada **dez** iterações (período que segue a "
"prática estabelecida de Benettin et al.). O MGS de espectro completo "
"acima é usado pelos wrappers de validação e, na varredura, para "
"recomputar as células marginais cuja classe a estimativa de vetor único "
"não resolve com confiança (fallback_mode=1)."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:54
msgid "Wolf et al. method"
msgstr "Método de Wolf et al."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:56
msgid ""
"Alan Wolf, Jack Swift, Harry Swinney, and John Vastano published the "
"canonical algorithm in 1985 [Wolf1985]_.  For a known map (as opposed to "
"a time series), the procedure is:"
msgstr "Alan Wolf, Jack Swift, Harry Swinney e John Vastano publicaram o algoritmo canônico em 1985 [Wolf1985]_.  Para um mapa conhecido (em vez de uma série temporal), o procedimento é:"

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:60
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Choose an initial condition :math:`\\mathbf{x}_0` on the attractor (in "
"our case, perturbed slightly around the fixed point)."
msgstr "Escolha uma condição inicial :math:`\\mathbf{x}_0` no atrator (no nosso caso, ligeiramente perturbada em torno do ponto fixo)."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:62
msgid "Initialise an orthonormal tangent basis :math:`W` (identity matrix)."
msgstr "Inicializa uma base tangente ortonormal :math:`W` (matriz identidade)."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:63
msgid "For :math:`k = 1` to :math:`N`:"
msgstr "Para :math:`k = 1` até :math:`N`:"

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:65
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Evolve the system: :math:`\\mathbf{x}_k = f(\\mathbf{x}_{k-1})`."
msgstr "Evolua o sistema: :math:`\\mathbf{x}_k = f(\\mathbf{x}_{k-1})`."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:66
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Evolve the tangent basis: :math:`Z = J(\\mathbf{x}_k) \\cdot W`."
msgstr "Evolua a base tangente: :math:`Z = J(\\mathbf{x}_k) \\cdot W`."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:67
msgid ""
"Apply Modified Gram-Schmidt to :math:`Z`, obtain orthonormal :math:`Q` "
"and the column norms :math:`n_i`."
msgstr ""
"Aplica Gram-Schmidt Modificado a :math:`Z`, obtém :math:`Q` ortonormal e "
"as normas das colunas :math:`n_i`."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:69
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Accumulate: :math:`\\lambda_i \\mathrel{+}= \\ln n_i`."
msgstr "Acumule: :math:`\\lambda_i \\mathrel{+}= \\ln n_i`."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:70
msgid "Replace :math:`W \\leftarrow Q`."
msgstr "Replace :math:`W \\leftarrow Q`."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:72
msgid "The Lyapunov spectrum is :math:`\\lambda_i / N`."
msgstr "O espectro de Lyapunov é :math:`\\lambda_i / N`."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:75
msgid "Pseudocode"
msgstr "Pseudocódigo"

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:104
msgid "Adaptations in ``chaotic-pfc``"
msgstr "Adaptações no ``chaotic-pfc``"

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:106
msgid ""
"**Modified Gram-Schmidt, not classical.**  Classical Gram-Schmidt "
"projects each vector against *all* preceding vectors at once; MGS "
"projects against one at a time and is more resistant to round-off error."
"  This is critical when the orbit visits regions where the Jacobian is "
"ill-conditioned."
msgstr "**Gram-Schmidt modificado, não o clássico.**  O Gram-Schmidt clássico projeta cada vetor contra *todos* os vetores precedentes de uma vez; o MGS projeta contra um de cada vez e é mais resistente a erros de arredondamento.  Isto é crítico quando a órbita visita regiões em que a Jacobiana é mal condicionada."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:111
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Underflow guard.**  The ``log(max(norm, 1e-300))`` clamp prevents "
"``log(0)`` (which would produce NaN) while being indistinguishable from "
"zero for any physically meaningful norm.  The constant :math:`10^{-300}` "
"was chosen well below machine underflow for ``float64`` (:math:`\\approx "
"10^{-308}` in subnormal range)."
msgstr "**Proteção contra underflow.**  O limitador ``log(max(norm, 1e-300))`` evita ``log(0)`` (que produziria NaN), sendo indistinguível de zero para qualquer norma fisicamente significativa.  A constante :math:`10^{-300}` foi escolhida bem abaixo do underflow de máquina para ``float64`` (:math:`\\approx 10^{-308}` na faixa subnormal)."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:117
msgid ""
"**Ensemble protocol.**  A single initial condition samples one "
"trajectory. To assess the **statistical robustness** of the Lyapunov "
"estimate, "
":func:`~chaotic_pfc.dynamics.lyapunov.lyapunov_henon2d_ensemble` draws "
":math:`N_{\\text{CI}}` independent initial conditions from a **centred** "
"uniform box (:math:`\\pm 10\\%`, as a fraction of each coordinate) around"
" the positive fixed point and computes the spectrum for each.  The output"
" (:class:`~chaotic_pfc.dynamics.lyapunov.EnsembleResult`) reports the "
"mean, maximum, and per-IC values, plus a count of how many ICs yield "
"positive :math:`\\lambda_{\\max}` (chaotic) versus non-positive "
"(periodic)."
msgstr ""
"**Protocolo de ensemble.**  Uma única condição inicial amostra uma "
"trajetória. Para avaliar a **robustez estatística** da estimativa de "
"Lyapunov, "
":func:`~chaotic_pfc.dynamics.lyapunov.lyapunov_henon2d_ensemble` sorteia "
":math:`N_{\\text{CI}}` condições iniciais independentes de uma caixa "
"uniforme **centrada** (:math:`\\pm 10\\%`, como fração de cada "
"coordenada) em torno do ponto fixo positivo e calcula o espectro para "
"cada uma.  A saída "
"(:class:`~chaotic_pfc.dynamics.lyapunov.EnsembleResult`) reporta a média,"
" o máximo e os valores por CI, além da contagem de quantas condições "
"iniciais produzem :math:`\\lambda_{\\max}` positivo (caótico) versus não "
"positivo (periódico)."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:127
msgid ""
"This is especially important when the attractor has multiple basins or "
"when the filter parameters push the system close to the chaos boundary."
msgstr ""
"Isso é especialmente importante quando o atrator tem múltiplas bacias ou "
"quando os parâmetros do filtro empurram o sistema para próximo da "
"fronteira do caos."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:131
msgid "Validation"
msgstr "Validação"

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:133
msgid ""
"The implementation has been validated against published reference values "
"from Wolf et al. (1985).  For the standard Hénon map :math:`(a = 1.4, b ="
" 0.3)`, our code with :math:`N_{\\text{itera}} = 20\\,000` yields "
":math:`\\lambda_1 = 0.417567` (Wolf reports :math:`0.418`, error "
":math:`0.10\\%`).  See :doc:`/validation` for the full validation report."
msgstr "A implementação foi validada contra valores de referência publicados por Wolf et al. (1985).  Para o mapa de Hénon padrão :math:`(a = 1.4, b = 0.3)`, nosso código com :math:`N_{\\text{itera}} = 20\\,000` produz :math:`\\lambda_1 = 0.417567` (Wolf reporta :math:`0.418`, erro :math:`0.10\\%`).  Veja :doc:`/validation` para o relatório completo."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:139
msgid ""
"A mathematical identity (:math:`\\lambda_1 + \\lambda_2 = \\ln|b|`) is "
"also verified routinely in the test suite (:ref:`validation`), confirming"
" correctness at machine precision independently of any published "
"reference."
msgstr ""
"A mathematical identity — :math:`\\lambda_1 + \\lambda_2 = \\ln|b|` — is "
"also verified routinely in the test suite (:ref:`validation`), confirming"
" correctness at machine precision independently of any published "
"reference."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:144
msgid "Known limitations"
msgstr "Limitações conhecidas"

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:146
msgid ""
"**Finite-time convergence.**  Published values correspond to :math:`N "
"\\to \\infty`.  With the sweep default of :math:`N = 3\\,000`, the "
"estimate can deviate by ~2–3% from the asymptotic value (the adaptive "
"early-stop may stop as early as :math:`N_{\\text{map,min}} = 500`).  The "
"sum identity :math:`\\lambda_1 + \\lambda_2 = \\ln|b|` remains exact at "
"any :math:`N`, confirming that the bias is a convergence-rate issue, not "
"a bug."
msgstr "**Convergência em tempo finito.**  Os valores publicados correspondem a :math:`N \\to \\infty`.  Com o padrão da varredura de :math:`N = 3\\,000`, a estimativa pode desviar ~2–3% do valor assintótico (a parada antecipada adaptativa pode parar já em :math:`N_{\\text{map,min}} = 500`).  A identidade da soma :math:`\\lambda_1 + \\lambda_2 = \\ln|b|` permanece exata em qualquer :math:`N`, confirmando que o viés é uma questão de taxa de convergência, não um bug."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:154
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Orbit divergence.**  Some parameter combinations cause the orbit to "
"diverge to infinity.  In those cases the QR loop produces NaN (instead of"
" the historical sentinel :math:`-1 \\times 10^{30}`).  NaN is the correct"
" mathematical answer : the exponent is undefined when the attractor does "
"not exist."
msgstr ""
"**Orbit divergence.**  Some parameter combinations cause the orbit to "
"diverge to infinity.  In those cases the QR loop produces NaN (instead of"
" the historical sentinel :math:`-1 \\times 10^{30}`).  NaN is the correct"
" mathematical answer — the exponent is undefined when the attractor does "
"not exist."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:160
msgid ""
"**QR cost.**  The :math:`O(D^3)` QR step is the bottleneck.  For the 4‑D "
"filtered system, each iteration is ~10× more expensive than for the 2‑D "
"standard map."
msgstr "**Custo do QR.**  O passo QR :math:`O(D^3)` é o gargalo.  Para o sistema filtrado 4-D, cada iteração é ~10× mais cara do que para o mapa padrão 2-D."

